{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:InformationTheory.PhaseTransitionBoundary","@type":"LeanModule","name":"InformationTheory.PhaseTransitionBoundary","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse","lean:module:QOU.MathConstants","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Linarith","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.NormNum","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Positivity","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.GCongr"],"declarations":15,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.SublimationCondition.halfFilled_implies_sublimes","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.SublimationCondition.halfFilled_implies_sublimes","kind":"theorem","line":128,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/phase-transition-boundary.lean#L128-L128","doc":"Half-filled shell with odd `Z` is the recorded sublimation pattern. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.SublimationCondition.sublimes","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.SublimationCondition.sublimes","kind":"def","line":126,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/phase-transition-boundary.lean#L126-L126","doc":"The atom sublimes. Left abstract: this file supplies no mechanism. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.SublimationCondition.shellCapacity","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.SublimationCondition.shellCapacity","kind":"def","line":124,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/phase-transition-boundary.lean#L124-L124","doc":"Capacity of the valence shell. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.SublimationCondition.valenceElectrons","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.SublimationCondition.valenceElectrons","kind":"def","line":122,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/phase-transition-boundary.lean#L122-L122","doc":"Number of valence electrons beyond last closed shell. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.SublimationCondition.crossingNumber","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.SublimationCondition.crossingNumber","kind":"def","line":120,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/phase-transition-boundary.lean#L120-L120","doc":"Crossing number of the composite atom. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.SublimationCondition.point","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.SublimationCondition.point","kind":"def","line":118,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/phase-transition-boundary.lean#L118-L118","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.SublimationCondition.sp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.SublimationCondition.sp","kind":"def","line":117,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/phase-transition-boundary.lean#L117-L117","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.SublimationCondition.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.SublimationCondition.mk","kind":"ctor","line":116,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/phase-transition-boundary.lean#L116-L116","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.SublimationCondition","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.SublimationCondition","kind":"structure","line":106,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/phase-transition-boundary.lean#L106-L131","doc":"**Sublimation condition** (type-level): the shell-and-parity pattern\n`rem:composite-crossing-sublimation-criteria` records, with the condition\nit implies left abstract.\n\nThe `sublimes` field is a bare `Prop` supplied by the instantiator. It was\nonce documented as \"the Hecke extension is non-split\"; that reading is\nwithdrawn (bean `qou-zut2`, 2026-08-24) because `Ext¹_{H_n(q)}` vanishes\nidentically away from roots of unity. Nothing here asserts what the\ncondition *is*, so the structure survives the withdrawal unchanged in\ncontent — only in name and documentation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.liquidSolid_lt_gasLiquid","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.liquidSolid_lt_gasLiquid","kind":"theorem","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/phase-transition-boundary.lean#L87-L104","doc":"The liquid-solid critical temperature is below the gas-liquid\ncritical temperature when [n_K]_q > 1. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.gasLiquidCriticalTemp_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.gasLiquidCriticalTemp_pos","kind":"theorem","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/phase-transition-boundary.lean#L65-L85","doc":"The gas-liquid critical temperature is positive when q > 1. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.liquidSolidCriticalTemp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.liquidSolidCriticalTemp","kind":"def","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/phase-transition-boundary.lean#L58-L63","doc":"**Liquid-solid critical temperature**.\nT_q^{l→s} = S_q^{∂} / ([2]_q · [n_K]_q).\nParameterised by the crossing number n_K and [n_K]_q. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.gasLiquidCriticalTemp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.gasLiquidCriticalTemp","kind":"def","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/phase-transition-boundary.lean#L52-L56","doc":"**Gas-liquid critical temperature**.\nT_q^{g→l} = S_q^{∂} / [2]_q. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:phase-transition-boundary","label":"prop:phase-transition-boundary","md":"quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/phase-transition-boundary.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.s3BoundaryAction","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.s3BoundaryAction","kind":"def","line":41,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/phase-transition-boundary.lean#L41-L50","doc":"**S³ boundary action**: the restriction of the categorical action\nto ∂(S³_q) ≅ S².  This is the energy cost of threading a knot\nthrough the fibre boundary.\nLabel: prop:phase-transition-boundary ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.R_q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.R_q","kind":"def","line":37,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/phase-transition-boundary.lean#L37-L39","doc":"Ground ring: archimedean specialisation `R_q := ℝ` (AGENTS.md §7c).\nThe numerical substrate value `q₀ ≈ 1.1097` lives in `ℝ`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}